s and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Hawaii remains one of the most Democratic states in presidential elections, and the Democratic nominee starts as a clear favorite here. The seat is open with a term-limited incumbent, so neither side benefits from incumbency, and the forecast rests almost entirely on the state's partisan lean rather than on candidate-specific evidence.\n\nNo public polls of the race, expert ratings, or market pricing are yet available, which keeps uncertainty wide. The one relevant local signal is an October survey showing Hawaii voters want Congress to check the president and trust Democrats more on key issues, a mild Democratic tailwind. That supports a small adjustment beyond the state's baseline lean. The Republican path runs through an unusually favorable national environment or a uniquely strong nominee; absent that, Hawaii is expected to stay in the Democratic column.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8703, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9295, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8784, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.877, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8862, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.878, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8719, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8743, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8792, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.879, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8843, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p